{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Like streams he stretches them out.</b> They lengthened and drew out to stretch far. Our Sages said: from the blessings of that wicked man we learn what was in his heart to curse them — when he said to set his face toward the wilderness, and when the Omnipresent turned his mouth, He blessed them from the substance of those curses he intended to say, etc., as is found in Ḥelek (Sanhedrin 105b)." "<b>Like aloes.</b> As the Targum renders — the language of ״מֹר וַאֲהָלוֹת״ (Psalms 45)." "<b>HaShem's planting.</b> In the Garden of Eden. Another interpretation: <b>Like aloes HaShem planted</b> — like the heavens stretched out like a tent." "<b>HaShem's planting.</b> We find the language of planting with tents, as it says ״וְיִטַּע אָהֳלֵי אַפַּדְנוֹ״ (Daniel 11)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:33.581728561Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}